# CLAUDE.local.md (personal — NOT committed)

Copy this file to `CLAUDE.local.md` and make it yours. It is git-ignored, so put machine-specific or
personal preferences here that should NOT be shared with the team. Keep it under ~200 lines. Claude
loads it automatically alongside `CLAUDE.md`; your personal rules win on conflict, so use sparingly.

## Examples of what goes here

- Which backend you point at locally (e.g. a teammate's tunnel) and the port you run Vite on.
- Personal workflow preferences ("show me the diff before committing", "run only the changed test").
- Scratch notes for your current task.

## Template (delete what you don't need)

```
## My environment
- Backend I run against: http://localhost:8000  (start it before `npm run dev`)
- Node version: 22 (matches CI)

## My preferences
- <e.g. always run `npm run lint && npm run typecheck` before proposing a commit>
- <e.g. prefer Testing Library queries by role/label>
```

Do NOT put secrets here. Public config goes in the documented `VITE_*` env vars (see `.env.example`).
